insert into public.questions (id,domain,question,options,explanation,simple) values
(1,'c','Which cloud benefit adds or removes resources automatically as demand changes?','["Elasticity","Geo-distribution","Reserved capacity","Data sovereignty"]'::jsonb,'Elasticity means resources grow and shrink with demand, so you only run what you need.','Like a rubber band that stretches only when something pulls on it.'),
(2,'c','In the shared responsibility model, what is always the customer’s responsibility, whatever the service type?','["Information and data","Physical datacenter security","Physical network","Host hardware"]'::jsonb,'Microsoft always secures the physical layer. Your data, accounts and identities stay yours in IaaS, PaaS and SaaS.','The landlord secures the building; you still lock your own flat.'),
(3,'c','A company stops buying servers and pays monthly for what it uses. Which shift is this?','["CapEx to OpEx","OpEx to CapEx","Private to hybrid","IaaS to on-premises"]'::jsonb,'Upfront hardware purchases are capital expenditure (CapEx). Pay-as-you-go cloud spending is operational expenditure (OpEx).','Buying a car (CapEx) versus paying for taxi rides (OpEx).'),
(4,'c','You manage only your apps and data, while Azure manages the OS and runtime. Which model is this?','["PaaS","IaaS","SaaS","On-premises"]'::jsonb,'With PaaS the provider handles servers, OS and runtime. IaaS leaves the OS to you; SaaS leaves only your data and settings.','A fully equipped kitchen: you bring ingredients and cook.'),
(5,'c','Which describes a hybrid cloud?','["On-premises datacenter combined with a public cloud","Two different public clouds only","Only a private cloud","A single Azure region"]'::jsonb,'Hybrid joins your own datacenter (private) with a public cloud so workloads can move between them.','Owning a house but renting a holiday flat when you need extra room.'),
(6,'a','What protects an app from the failure of one datacenter inside an Azure region?','["Availability zones","Resource locks","Azure Policy","Management groups"]'::jsonb,'Availability zones are separate datacenters in a region, each with its own power, cooling and networking.','Keeping spare keys in three different buildings.'),
(7,'a','Which service runs small pieces of code triggered by events, without managing servers?','["Azure Functions","Azure Virtual Machines","Azure Bastion","Azure Backup"]'::jsonb,'Azure Functions is serverless compute. You pay only while the code runs.','A vending machine: it works only when someone presses a button.'),
(8,'a','Azure Blob Storage is best suited for which type of data?','["Unstructured data such as images and videos","Relational tables only","Message queues only","Virtual machine CPUs"]'::jsonb,'Blob storage holds massive amounts of unstructured objects like files, media and backups.','A huge warehouse where you drop boxes of any shape.'),
(9,'a','Which service creates an encrypted tunnel between your network and Azure over the public internet?','["VPN Gateway","ExpressRoute","Azure Firewall","Load Balancer"]'::jsonb,'VPN Gateway uses the internet. ExpressRoute is a private connection that does not cross the public internet.','A tinted-window car on a public road, not a private railway.'),
(10,'a','What is a logical container that groups related Azure resources for shared management?','["Resource group","Region","Availability set","Virtual network"]'::jsonb,'A resource group holds resources that share a lifecycle, so you can deploy, manage and delete them together.','A folder for everything one project needs.'),
(11,'m','Which tool estimates the cost of Azure services before you deploy them?','["Pricing calculator","Azure Advisor","Service Health","Azure Monitor"]'::jsonb,'The Pricing calculator forecasts costs for planned resources. The TCO calculator compares Azure with on-premises costs.','A shopping basket total before you reach the till.'),
(12,'m','What does Azure Policy do?','["Enforces rules such as allowed regions on resources","Stores secrets","Balances web traffic","Backs up virtual machines"]'::jsonb,'Azure Policy evaluates resources against your standards and can block or flag those that do not comply.','House rules that say which pets are allowed.'),
(13,'m','What is the purpose of a resource lock?','["Prevent accidental deletion or changes","Encrypt data at rest","Reduce costs","Move resources between regions"]'::jsonb,'CanNotDelete and ReadOnly locks protect resources even from users who have permission to change them.','A safety cover over a light switch.'),
(14,'m','Which feature asks users for a second proof of identity, such as a phone prompt?','["Multi-factor authentication","Resource tags","Network peering","Azure Blueprints"]'::jsonb,'MFA requires two or more verification methods, so a stolen password alone is not enough. It is part of Microsoft Entra ID.','A bank card plus a PIN.'),
(15,'m','Which service gives personalised recommendations on cost, security, reliability and performance?','["Azure Advisor","Azure Policy","Azure Lighthouse","Azure Arc"]'::jsonb,'Azure Advisor analyses your resources and suggests ways to improve them.','A personal trainer reviewing your workout.'),
(16,'c','Which benefit keeps services running with minimal downtime, backed by an SLA?','["High availability","Predictable licensing","Data residency","Hardware ownership"]'::jsonb,'High availability means services stay reachable even when parts of the system fail.','A shop with a backup generator.'),
(17,'c','Which pricing approach means you pay only for the resources you actually use?','["Consumption-based","Fixed annual licence","Hardware depreciation","Perpetual purchase"]'::jsonb,'Consumption-based pricing charges for usage, so there is no large upfront spend.','A prepaid phone plan billed per minute used.'),
(18,'c','Which cloud type is owned and used by a single organisation?','["Private cloud","Public cloud","Multi-tenant cloud","Shared cloud"]'::jsonb,'A private cloud is dedicated to one organisation, on-premises or hosted.','A private members-only club.'),
(19,'c','A company uses Microsoft 365 email without managing servers or software. Which model is this?','["SaaS","IaaS","PaaS","On-premises"]'::jsonb,'SaaS delivers a finished application. You just use it and manage your data and users.','Taking a taxi instead of owning a car.'),
(20,'c','Who patches the guest operating system on an Azure virtual machine (IaaS)?','["The customer","Microsoft","The internet provider","Nobody, it is automatic"]'::jsonb,'In IaaS Microsoft manages the physical host. You manage the OS, patches and apps on the VM.','You rent the empty flat; the furniture is yours to fix.'),
(21,'a','Which service hosts web apps without you managing the underlying servers?','["Azure App Service","Azure Bastion","Azure DNS","Azure Backup"]'::jsonb,'App Service is a PaaS offering for web apps and APIs, with built-in scaling.','A food court stall: the building is already run for you.'),
(22,'a','Which Blob access tier is cheapest for data you rarely read and can wait hours to get back?','["Archive","Hot","Premium","Standard SSD"]'::jsonb,'Archive is the lowest-cost tier, but retrieving data takes hours.','Winter clothes stored in the loft.'),
(23,'a','Which service gives a private, dedicated connection to Azure that avoids the public internet?','["ExpressRoute","VPN Gateway","Azure Front Door","Traffic Manager"]'::jsonb,'ExpressRoute uses a connectivity provider for a private link with more reliability and consistent speeds.','A private railway line between two cities.'),
(24,'a','What is the purpose of an Azure region pair?','["Disaster recovery between two regions in the same geography","Combining two subscriptions","Doubling a VM’s size","Merging billing accounts"]'::jsonb,'Each region is paired with another in the same geography, so recovery is possible if a whole region fails.','A sister branch that can take over if one shop closes.'),
(25,'a','Which service runs a container quickly without managing virtual machines?','["Azure Container Instances","Azure DNS","Azure Advisor","Azure Policy"]'::jsonb,'Azure Container Instances starts containers in seconds with no servers to manage.','Pop-up shops that open and close on demand.'),
(26,'a','Which service is a managed relational database for SQL Server workloads?','["Azure SQL Database","Azure Blob Storage","Azure Queue Storage","Azure Files"]'::jsonb,'Azure SQL Database is a PaaS relational database with built-in backups and patching.','A filing cabinet someone else maintains.'),
(27,'a','Which service spreads incoming traffic across several virtual machines?','["Azure Load Balancer","Azure Key Vault","Azure Monitor","Azure Backup"]'::jsonb,'A load balancer distributes requests so no single VM is overwhelmed and failures are tolerated.','A host sending guests to free tables.'),
(28,'a','Which is the correct hierarchy, from the top down?','["Management groups, subscriptions, resource groups, resources","Subscriptions, management groups, resources, resource groups","Resource groups, subscriptions, management groups, resources","Resources, resource groups, subscriptions, management groups"]'::jsonb,'Management groups hold subscriptions, which hold resource groups, which hold resources.','Country, city, street, house.'),
(29,'a','Which cross-platform command-line tool manages Azure resources?','["Azure CLI","Azure Advisor","Azure Service Health","Azure Monitor"]'::jsonb,'Azure CLI and Azure PowerShell let you script and automate Azure tasks.','Typing commands instead of clicking buttons.'),
(30,'a','Which service offers file shares accessed over SMB?','["Azure Files","Azure Queue Storage","Azure Table Storage","Azure DNS"]'::jsonb,'Azure Files provides fully managed cloud file shares, similar to a network drive.','A shared drive in the cloud.'),
(31,'m','Which tool compares the cost of running workloads on-premises with running them in Azure?','["TCO calculator","Pricing calculator","Azure Monitor","Service Health"]'::jsonb,'The TCO calculator estimates savings from moving to Azure. The Pricing calculator prices specific Azure resources.','Comparing the cost of owning a car with using taxis.'),
(32,'m','Which feature controls what users can do by assigning roles at a scope?','["Azure RBAC","Resource tags","Azure Advisor","Network peering"]'::jsonb,'Role-based access control assigns roles such as Reader or Contributor to users at a chosen scope.','Staff badges that open only certain doors.'),
(33,'m','Which service tells you about Azure incidents affecting the services and regions you use?','["Azure Service Health","Azure Advisor","Azure Policy","Microsoft Cost Management"]'::jsonb,'Service Health gives personalised alerts about outages, planned maintenance and advisories.','A traffic report for your own route.'),
(34,'m','Which service collects and analyses metrics and logs from your resources?','["Azure Monitor","Azure Policy","Azure Blueprints","Azure Backup"]'::jsonb,'Azure Monitor gathers telemetry so you can see performance and set alerts.','A dashboard in a car.'),
(35,'m','Which feature helps organise resources for cost reporting, for example by department?','["Tags","Locks","Availability zones","Virtual networks"]'::jsonb,'Tags are name-value labels. They help group resources for billing and management.','Colour-coded sticky notes.'),
(36,'m','Which service lets you analyse spending and set budgets across Azure?','["Microsoft Cost Management","Azure Advisor","Azure Arc","Azure DNS"]'::jsonb,'Cost Management helps you monitor, allocate and control cloud spending with budgets and alerts.','A banking app for your cloud bill.'),
(37,'m','Which Microsoft Entra ID capability lets users sign in once to reach many apps?','["Single sign-on","Resource locks","Availability sets","Pay-as-you-go"]'::jsonb,'Single sign-on (SSO) means one identity gives access to many applications.','One key card for the whole office.'),
(38,'m','Where can you find Microsoft’s compliance reports and audit documents?','["Service Trust Portal","Azure Marketplace","Azure Advisor","Azure Status page"]'::jsonb,'The Service Trust Portal publishes certifications, audit reports and compliance guidance.','A library of safety inspection certificates.'),
(39,'m','Which service lets you manage on-premises and multi-cloud servers from Azure?','["Azure Arc","Azure Bastion","Azure Functions","Azure DNS"]'::jsonb,'Azure Arc extends Azure management and governance to resources running outside Azure.','A universal remote for devices everywhere.'),
(40,'m','Which security principle gives users only the access they need to do their job?','["Least privilege","Shared accounts","Open access by default","Global admin for everyone"]'::jsonb,'Least privilege limits damage if an account is compromised, because it can do very little.','A visitor pass that opens only the meeting room.');
